(3. FORMATIVE ASSESSMENT MODELS AND STUDENT AGENCY) '
() '
(Formative assessments serve as diagnostic compasses rather than) '
(punitive evaluations. When educators deploy frequent low-stakes) '
(self-assessments, student test anxiety metrics decrease by 41%) '
(across introductory STEM sequences.) '
() '
(Furthermore, student agency is significantly bolstered when learners) '
(are permitted to select modular project themes that intersect with) '
(community-based experiential inquiries. Capstone evaluations) '
(revealed superior analytical depth in cohorts utilizing self-) '
(selected project rubrics compared to rigid uniform testing cohorts.) '
() '
(4. SOCIO-EMOTIONAL FACTORS AND FACULTY MENTORSHIP IMPACT) '
() '
(Qualitative interviews conducted across 450 undergraduate students) '
(highlighted that regular proactive check-ins from academic advisors) '
(and teaching assistants correlated with an 89% semester completion) '
(rate.) '
() '
(Underrepresented student demographics experienced the highest) '
(proportional retention gains when matched with faculty mentorship) '
(circles during their foundational semester.) '
() '
ET

endstream
